From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kristof Imeri <kristof@lanth.me>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 04:30:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 36/50] clutter: draw text and offscreen textures at the view's
 own scale on whole pixels

On a view with a fractional scale such as 1.5, resources were made at the
scale rounded up to 2 and shrunk by linear filtering when painted, so text
and icons came out soft, and softer still wherever an actor's position fell
between device pixels, as it does for most popups and labels.

Lay text out and size offscreen effects at the actor's unrounded resource
scale, and move text layouts and textures that map one texel to one device
pixel onto whole pixels when they are painted. Scaled or rotated actors,
such as those in an animation that zooms, keep their exact position.
